  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "If $\\tan (\\cot x)=\\cot (\\tan x)$, then $\\sin 2 x$ is equal to:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "z4GVw",
      "text": "$\\frac{2}{(2 n+1) \\pi}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "TV9Rf",
      "text": "$\\frac{4}{(2 n+1) \\pi}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "ZRSUG",
      "text": "$\\frac{2}{n(n+1) \\pi}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "i8itz",
      "text": "$\\frac{4}{n(n+1) \\pi}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given, $\\tan (\\cot x)=\\cot (\\tan x)=\\tan \\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}-\\tan x\\right)$\r\n\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\cot x=n \\pi+\\frac{\\pi}{2}-\\tan x$\r\n\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\cot x+\\tan x=n \\pi+\\frac{\\pi}{2}$\r\n\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\frac{1}{\\sin x \\cos x}=n \\pi+\\frac{\\pi}{2} \\Rightarrow \\frac{1}{\\sin 2 x}=\\frac{n \\pi}{2}+\\frac{\\pi}{4}$\r\n\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\sin 2 x=\\frac{1}{\\frac{n \\pi}{2}+\\frac{\\pi}{4}}=\\frac{4}{(2 n+1) \\pi}$",
    "image": null
  },
